<h1>Transforming events in flight</h1>
<p>As <a href="/concepts-events">events</a> flow from a source connector to a destination in a <a href="/concepts-pipelines">pipeline</a>, you can transform them in real time. Transforms allow you to reshape data structures, discard irrelevant records, and enrich events with additional context before they reach storage or downstream consumers.</p>

<h2>How transforms work</h2>
<p>Transforms run sequentially in the order defined in the pipeline's <code>transforms</code> array. Each step accepts the output of the previous step, modifies or evaluates the event, and passes the result along to the next step. If all transforms succeed, the resulting event is written to the des
